            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PeppyCod4089"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic with just a few tweaks!!! In addition to the optional honey, I added 1/2 a mashed banana &amp; 1 Tbsp of Greek yogurt to prevent dryness. I also used the batter in a cupcake tin (vs the 6-cup mold ring), which yielded 10 cupcakes total, and baked perfectly in 20 mins. For the grand finale, I iced them with a mixture of 1/4 cup peanut butter &amp; 1/3 cup of Greek yogurt. They were absolute hit with my birthday beagle!",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-26T15:07:23.822Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scott"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Adapted for \"pup-cakes\"--used half of an over-ripe banana for sweetener instead of honey. Baking time was only 20 minutes. Topped with vanilla yogurt and a blueberry. Made a dozen.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-25T03:56:28.986Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kyla Duffy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great for people and pets! I made the recipe without honey, reserved 1/4, and doled the rest out into cupcake cups. I added a few TBSP agave to the 1/4 I reserved and baked it all up. It only took 20 minutes in the oven. The cupcakes with agave were delicious, and the dogs loved the ones without.",
            "datePublished": "2017-05-16T11:53:29.900Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LovingRoe8030"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was very delicious and my dog Merle loved it! However, vanilla extract has alcohol which is toxic to dogs, so I left that out as well as baking soda because that is also toxic.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-23T17:40:50.975Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
