              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Our dogs loved it! Used a squirt of real whipped cream and a peanut butter dog bone on top of each party dog’s slice. Didn’t change anything, but I got Julienne cut carrots and ended up having to mash them up a little with a stick mixer. Must have made it juicier. Cooked 22 minutes.",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-24T03:01:52.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "YumYum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe made these into 8 regular sized muffin / cupcakes ( pup-cakes). Substituted apple sauce for the oil. Baked for about 25 min, but that was too long. I would say these are done in about 15 to 20 minutes. 25 made them a little too dry on the inside, but my dog still devoured it :)\nMade a frosting out of cream cheese, peanut butter, and honey. Used one 8 oz block of cream cheese, one cup of peanut butter, and about 1/4 cup of honey to make the frosting. Will post picture :)",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-06T09:28:46.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Natasha Jade Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made these and love them, for my dog and even myself. I used apple sauce instead of oil, mashed two bananas instead of carrots and I did add in some organic solid honey and added extra flour for the right consistency for muffins. Cut cooking time in half, used muffin tin and made 8 muffins. I filled the cups full and they puffed up nicely.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-30T22:07:01.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HonestPlum1591"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My granddaughter and I made this for our pups first birthday. She (5) had a really good time mixing and measuring. We made them as muffins in cupcake papers. We called them “pup cakes”. We substituted unsweetened applesauce for the oil. They were perfectly done in 20 minutes. We iced the ones we ate with buttercream frosting. DEELICIOUS!",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-09T18:07:47.579Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
